            <ArticleTitle>[Unusual case of headache of psychogenic origin].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>701-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of attacks of short-lasting pains in the midfrontal region is reported. The attacks occurred several dozen of times per day, no drugs were effective. Contrast radiological investigations failed to show presence of an expanding lesion. After psychotherapy (suggestion reinforced with faradic current) the attacks disappeared completely.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
